==Description== <!--T:2-->

<!--T:3-->
This macro provides a dialog interface to rotate the 3D view to precise absolute angles. Unlike the default view rotations (top, front, right, etc.), this macro allows you to specify exact rotation angles around the X, Y, and Z axes, giving you full control over the viewing angle.

==Usage== <!--T:4-->

<!--T:5-->
# Run the macro from the Macro menu
# A dialog window will appear with three spin boxes for:
#* **Alpha**: Rotation around the Z axis (0-360 degrees)
#* **Beta**: Rotation around the Y axis (0-180 degrees)
#* **Gamma**: Rotation around the X axis (0-360 degrees)
# Adjust the values to your desired viewing angle
# Click **OK** to apply the rotation
# The 3D view will immediately update to the specified angles

